abstract: >-
  Code, trained detectors and simulation inputs for an integrated fault
  detection and compensation framework for hydronic radiator faults in
  district-heated buildings. Three unsupervised anomaly detectors, trained only
  on a fault-free heating season, run inside the EnergyPlus solver through the
  Python API. A signature-based ladder classifies the detected anomaly as a
  stuck-closed valve, a zone-level over-delivery setpoint bias, or a
  system-level supply-temperature setpoint bias, and a supervisory controller
  adjusts the district-heating supply setpoint accordingly within the same
  simulation. The repository covers detector training, the in-the-loop runtime,
  the severity and compensation-parameter sweeps, the compound-fault stress
  tests, and the analysis that produces the reported tables.
